  "body": "**Stacked on #644**, which is stacked on #640. Review only this PR's own commit, `0f94a534`.\n\n**P1 (#650):** #640 reads LinuxCNC's 1-9 orientation chart in the **front-turret** frame. Tormach PathPilot, a rear tool with X+ toward the tool, numbers the same physical tools mirrored in X: 1↔4, 2↔3, 6↔8, with 5, 7 and 9 unchanged. A PathPilot user entering their tool table's 3 would get the boring-bar tip.\n\n## Evidence\nThese are the contributor's PathPilot Hub 8L v2.14.4 conversational samples, used as behaviour reference only.\n- **(a) Facing with orientation 3 to centre:** fits only the mirror (rear 3 = front 2, tip (−X, −Z)).\n- **(b) External thread wants 8:** fits only the mirror (rear 8 = front 6, tip at the axis).\n- **(c) A chamfer refusing 3 with [1,5,6] / [2,6,7]:** fits the mirror only if PathPilot treated that chamfer as **internal**. Unmirrored, those are the OD chamfer sets.\n  - Not forced. **Recorded and open:** one Hub check of an explicit OD chamfer with tool 3. If PathPilot still refuses it, the reading must be revisited before #626 relies on it.\n\n## What changed\n- **Machine key `general.turret`,** `front` or `rear`:\n  - absent means front, and any other word is refused by name;\n  - an editor field and the validator;\n  - the built-in Lathe states `front`.\n  - No Tormach lathe `.mch` exists yet, so none is marked rear.\n- **Tools store the front-frame (canonical) code, the physical tool;** each machine **shows** its own number. A tool keeps its physical meaning across machines, and front projects and all front goldens are byte-identical.\n- **`crates/tools/src/turret.rs`** handles the renumbering, the fitting lists, labels and captions.\n- **Where the frame applies:** the post uses the op's own setup's machine.\n  - The refusals, the defaults (OD 2 front / 3 rear; boring bar 3 / 2; blade left corner 2 / 3; blade codes [1,2,6] / [3,4,8]), the editor row and the `ORIENTATION q` note all use that machine's numbers.\n  - Refusals are tagged \"(front|rear turret numbering)\".\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/650-turret-side.md`. It supersedes #640's line that the number doesn't depend on the turret side.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `lathe_turret_side` (7):**\n  - rear 3 posts exactly front 2's path, and the rear default matches;\n  - a rear facing with 3 reaches centre, pinned by a new golden `facing_rear.nc` (identical to `facing.nc` except for the note's number);\n  - rear 8 posts (−r, 0), and rear 6 is refused with rear numbers;\n  - each machine's refusal lists use its own numbers;\n  - the chamfer data point under the mirror reading;\n  - the `.mch` key parse and refusal;\n  - a rear project round-trips byte-identical.\n- **Also new:** `lathe_blade_corner::a_rear_turret_numbers_the_corners_in_its_own_frame`, tools `turret` units (4), and the ui orientation row's rear frame.\n- **Gate:**\n  - all 46 app binaries pass: lathe_*, turning_*, machine*, tool_*, tormach_*, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, conformance, golden_cl, posting;\n  - tools lib 39 and post 55 pass;\n  - clippy is clean on 4 crates.\n\n## Not exercised (why this is a draft)\nThe Hub OD-chamfer check in (c).\n\nChangelog: Lathe tool orientation numbers are read in the machine's turret frame: a `.mch` states `general.turret` (front|rear, default front), so a rear-turret lathe's OD tool 3 / OD thread tip 8 posts the same control point as a front lathe's 2 / 6, and refusals, defaults, the tool editor and the tool note use that machine's numbers (#650)\n\nFixes #650\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
